# Provider probes. Deployed by CI to /etc/cron.d/model-checks.
# flock prevents overlapping runs; timeout kills a stuck job before the next one starts.
#
# The benchmark is NOT here: it runs on a Temporal schedule (smolevich-bench-2x-daily,
# 07:00/19:00 UTC) executed by smolevich-bench-worker.service. A cron drain stood behind it
# from 14 to 17 August and never picked up a single job across six clean runs, so it is gone.
# To fall back to cron, restore:
#   0 7,19 * * * root flock -n /var/lock/mbench.lock timeout 1800 \
#     /bin/sh -c '... model-benchmark run --max-jobs 200 ...'
# and pause the schedule, or both will enqueue the same batch.
#
# The probes stay on cron on purpose: seconds of work every ten minutes, nothing to make
# durable, and moving them would add ~1500 Temporal actions a day for no gain.
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin

*/10 * * * * root  flock -n /var/lock/mhc.lock    timeout 540   /usr/local/bin/model-health-check  >> /var/log/model-health-check.log  2>&1
*/15 * * * * root  flock -n /var/lock/mac.lock    timeout 540   /usr/local/bin/model-audio-check   >> /var/log/model-audio-check.log   2>&1
*/15 * * * * root  flock -n /var/lock/mmc.lock    timeout 540   /usr/local/bin/model-media-check   >> /var/log/model-media-check.log   2>&1
